   "definition_quote": "At each time slot $t$, each client $i$ observes a context $c_{i,t}\\in\\mathcal{C}$ drawn according to distribution $\\rho_i\\in\\mathcal{P}$. Then, client $i$ pulls arm $a_{i,t}\\in\\mathcal{A}$ and receives a reward $r_{i,t} = \\phi(c_{i,t},a_{i,t})^{\\TT}\\theta^* + \\eta_{i,t}$, where $\\theta^*\\in\\Rb^d$ is an unknown parameter vector shared among clients, $\\eta_{i,t}$ is a random noise, and $\\phi(c_{i,t},a_{i,t})\\in \\Rb^d$ is the feature vector associated with arm $a_{i,t}$ and context $c_{i,t}$. For simplicity, we denote $\\phi(c_{i,t},a)$ as $x_{i,t,a}$. \nWe assume $\\|\\phi(c,a)\\|_2\\leq 1$, $\\|\\theta^*\\|_2\\leq 1$, and $\\eta_{i,t}$ is an IID standard Gaussian random variable, i.e., $\\eta_{i,t}\\sim N(0,1)$."
  },
